      "content": "Certainly, here's a preliminary clinical summary for the attending:\n\n\"The 64-year-old male patient presented with acute onset shortness of breath and chest tightness. Vitals revealed a blood pressure of 145/92, heart rate of 102, and oxygen saturation of 93% on room air. He has a history of smoking (30 pack-years), hypertension, and Type 2 Diabetes. Physical examination findings include slight diaphoresis and bilateral crackles in the lower lung lobes. The EKG showed sinus tachycardia without ST-elevation. Current possible differentials include pulmonary embolism, acute coronary syndrome, or pulmonary edema. Troponin levels are pending.\"",
